 "observations": [
  "The page number «195» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 80», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature «25*» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The title (L01), «Aequatio casarum duodecim signo tauri», the equation of the twelve houses for the sign of Taurus, in bold, without sigla. The folios of the manuscripts stand at the right of the title in two lines, «C 87r, O 143v,» and «N 50v.», the letters raised; here as right margin notes beside L01 and L02.",
  "The table: as on p. 194 (JP2 0226), the degrees of the ascendant, «Gradus aequales ortus tauri», in four lines, and five pairs «Gr.», «Min.» under «Secundum Taurus1) [et Gemini]», «Tertium Gemini [et Cancer]», «Quartum Cancer [et Leo]», «Quintum Leo [et Virgo]» and «Sextum Virgo1) [et Libra]», the names of the signs in the heads from N (note 1). Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L02-L05); the units in L06; the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The names of the signs into which the beginnings of the houses pass stand in lines of their own over their columns: «Gemini» (L10) over the second house, «Libra» (L14, note r) over the sixth, «Cancer» (L19) over the third, «Virgo» (L23) over the fifth and «Leo» (L30) over the fourth.",
  "L07-L41. The beginnings of the second to the sixth house for the ascendant at 1° to 30° of Taurus, by the rule of p. 194. Checked against the beginnings computed as there, with the obliquity 23° 35′ and the latitude 38° 40′: the values of the rows 1° to 26° agree within 2.5′ except at 19° in the fourth house (L29), Cancer 29° 45′ for 29° 38.3′, 6.7′ more. From 27° to 30° (L38-L41) all five columns fall behind the computation, by 2.7′ to 5.2′ at 27°, 3.4′ to 9.2′ at 28°, 5.2′ to 13.8′ at 29° and 7.2′ to 19.0′ at 30°, most in the fourth house: their steps stay those of the preceding rows (51′ in the second house, 44′ in the fourth), where the computed ones grow (53′, 48′ to 49′). In the next table, p. 196 (JP2 0228), the first row, 1° of Gemini, has the second to the sixth house at 23° 33′, 15° 45′, 8° 45′, 15° 58′ and 24° 49′ of their signs, 61′, 55′, 55′, 63′ and 65′ after the 30° of this page.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the computation: the edition's readings are the nearer at 2° in the second house (note a: O's 28° 43′ against C's 48; 28° 43.6′ computed), at 12° and 19° in the third (notes b and c: O's 0 and C's 6 in the degrees, against C's 1 and O's 5; 0° 53.1′ and 6° 10.1′), at 3° and 14° in the fourth (notes i and l: C's 52 against O's 51 and O's 4 against C's 3; 18° 53.1′ and 26° 5.9′), and at 11°, 13° and 18° in the fifth (notes o, n and p: C's 58 against O's 18, C's 29 against O's 19 in the degrees, C's 58 against O's 57; 27° 57.6′, 29° 38.5′, 3° 58.2′); the degrees of notes e, f, g and h (14°, 19°, 23° and 26° in the fourth house: O's 26, C's 29, C's 2 and O's 4 against C's 25, O's 19, O's 3 and C's 5) are those that the order of the column requires. At 21° in the third house, 8° in the fourth and 19° in the fifth (notes d, k and q) the computation lies half a minute from both readings (7° 43.5′, 22° 4.5′, 4° 51.5′). At 28° in the fourth house (note m) O's 22, the edition's reading, keeps the steps of the column, 44′ and 44′, where C's 26 gives 48′ and 40′; the computation, 6° 31.2′, lies in the stretch of the table that falls behind it.",
  "Notes 1 and r: the names of the signs in the heads from Taurus to Virgo are N's, omitted in C and O; O omits «Libra» (L14). Italics: «om.». N01: «Taurus. . . .Virgo», the points of the lemma as printed."
 ],
